.Nd async event loop abstraction with sd-event and libevent backends
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/event.h
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_ev_new_default "struct mbt_ev **out"
.Ft int
.Op "HAVE_SD_EVENT"
.Fn mbt_ev_sd_new "struct mbt_ev **out"
.Ft int
.Op "HAVE_SD_EVENT"
.Cm "struct sd_event *"
.Fn mbt_ev_sd_new_from "struct mbt_ev **out" "struct sd_event *loop"
.Ft int
.Op "HAVE_LIBEVENT"
.Fn mbt_ev_libevent_new "struct mbt_ev **out"
.Ft int
.Op "HAVE_LIBEVENT"
.Cm "struct event_base *"
.Fn mbt_ev_libevent_new_from "struct mbt_ev **out" "struct event_base *base"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_ev_run "const struct mbt_ev *ev"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_ev_stop "const struct mbt_ev *ev"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_ev_destroy "struct mbt_ev *ev"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_ev_io_new "struct mbt_ev *ev" "struct mbt_ev_io **out" "int fd" "uint32_t events" "mbt_ev_io_cb cb" "void *arg"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_ev_io_mod "struct mbt_ev_io *io" "uint32_t events"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_ev_io_free "struct mbt_ev_io *io"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_ev_timer_new "struct mbt_ev *ev" "struct mbt_ev_timer **out" "uint64_t usec" "mbt_ev_timer_cb cb" "void *arg"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_ev_timer_mod "struct mbt_ev_timer *timer" "uint64_t usec"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_ev_timer_free "struct mbt_ev_timer *timer"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The event loop abstraction provides platform-independent async I/O and timer support.
Callers select a backend at compile time via Meson or supply their own event base.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_ev_new_default
creates an event loop using whichever backend is compiled in.
.Fn mbt_ev_sd_new
uses sd-event (systemd event loop) when available;
.Fn mbt_ev_libevent_new
uses libevent.
The
.Ql _new_from
variants wrap an externally-owned event base, enabling integration with applications that manage their own loops.
.Ss I/O watches
.Fn mbt_ev_io_new
registers interest in a file descriptor for read and/or write events
(defined by the
.Va MBT_EV_READ / Va MBT_EV_WRITE
bitmask passed through
.Fa events ).
The callback fires when readable or writable depending on mask.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_ev_io_mod
changes the event mask without re-creating the watch.
.Fn mbt_ev_io_free
deregisters and frees it.
.Ss Timers
.Fn mbt_ev_timer_new
creates an absolute timer firing once after
.Fa usec
microseconds elapse, invoking its callback.
.Fn mbt_ev_timer_mod
reschedules it for a new absolute time value.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Ft int
return 0 on success or a negative errno value on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt_session 3 ,
.Xr mbt_conn 3
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Nick Owens Aq Mt mischief@offblast.org
.Sh POLLABLE BACKEND
The pollable backend allows integrating libmbt into an external event loop.
The caller drives the loop with
.Xr poll 2
or any equivalent mechanism (libuv, gio, kqueue wrapper, etc.).
.Pp
.Fn mbt_ev_new_pollable
creates an event loop that does not own a run loop.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_ev_pollfd
fills the provided
.Fa fds
array with file descriptors and event masks.
Returns the number of entries written (up to
.Fa max ) .
.Pp
.Fn mbt_ev_timeout_ms
returns the number of milliseconds until the next timer fires,
or \-1 if no timers are active.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_ev_dispatch
processes fired events from the
.Fa fds
array (after poll returns) and fires any expired timers.
.Pp
Typical usage:
.Bd -literal
struct mbt_ev *ev;
mbt_ev_new_pollable(&ev);
/* ... register IOs and timers via mbt_session_new etc ... */

while (running) {
    struct pollfd fds[64];
    int n = mbt_ev_pollfd(ev, fds, 64);
    int ms = mbt_ev_timeout_ms(ev);
    poll(fds, n, ms);
    mbt_ev_dispatch(ev, fds, n);
}
.Ed
